Use of git add src/cavendish_particle_tracks/merge_unmerge_csv.py merges CSV files (made from pds) into one bigger CSV file. It would be much better to merge in pandas and then write a single CSV file, skipping the internal roundrripping via CSV.  Should fix in long term but no time now.

Also the way _setup_calibration_layers is used in _calibration manager is really icky. (it is half defauly constructor, half load from file, it is a mess). Fix 

We would like to persistify points like start or decay vertices in the calibration file. However this would require creation of stable process IDs which do not currently exist.

Should add ability to remove origin/ecay vertex from current process.

When image data is loaded late, the bubble chamber layer becomes very large.

The process table seems to have a visual part and an internal data part, and the two are kept in sync by duplicate insertions and removals. This seems fragile.  Much better owuld be to have one core representation and multiple views of it.

Move most simple messages to the same format used after successful file save: napari.utils.notifications.show_info("Data saved to " + file_name)

At present one is not allowed to save data when the table is empty (no data) ... even though the "you have unsaved data" may trigger if there were previous rows that have since been deleted. Getting rid of the inability to save empty data would be good!

At the moment you can clone all forms of A' (i.e. all three views) into the event, but this may not be what you want to do!  You may only want to do it for THIS view!

Points in the event calib layer don't show their fidicual labels.  AND there is nothing to stop many of them being created in overlap with each other.

Users should be able to choose where calibrations get saved.

Meta is not yet checked in the calibrations dirty accounting. It should be.

The cloning of fid points into the event layer prevents inserting duplicates, but if you insert all views at once it may insert non-duplicates in some views and then hit a missing part, making for an incomplete operation. I.e. although duplicates will not be inserted, it is possible that a PARTIAL insertion will occur when really the user would prefer an all-success or all-failure outcome. So should validate earlier.
